A||||13||FIEROCIOUS||Header Paint Durability???||||1||
Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||05-18-2000||12:10 AM||||How well does the paint/powder coat on the Fiero Stores Sprint monifolds hold up?<P>Does it burn off instantly or is it fairly scratch, rust, and abuse resistant?<P>Do you have a set?<BR>how long have you had them?<BR>Have you had them off since you installed them?<BR>Does the finish become dull?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||05-18-2000||08:35 AM||||not sure about the Fiero Stores units.. but for less money you can have a nicer looking bigger piped set from Chris West. I had mine sent to Jet Hot for their Thermal Protective barrier coating. it's guarranteed for 3600*F and will not change colors or flake off. I'll post a pick later tonite...  to chris west... <A HREF="http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/Exhaust/Exhaust.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/Exhaust/Exhaust.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RiceCooker||05-18-2000||07:24 PM||||I would love to know if anyone else has the sprint manifolds too. Mine are getting put on as we speak. I'm also getting the cat converter taken off too. I'll let everyone know how it goes when I get back from the long weekend. (Canadian)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIEROCIOUS||05-19-2000||02:24 AM||||To late already bought mine they are sitting on my desk as of now.<P>I've read all the information on headers and it makes me kinda laugh, stagger tuned ect. and all the argument about the Fiero Stores headers. <P>Not to spark any flames but,... <P>How many of you that tout "equal length headers are better" have actualy seen equal length headers on a street car?<P>I for one have never I repeat NEVER have. <P>Most headers are a compromise of length and fit. Anyone remember 180 headers? they are not equal length, I have however seen equal length headers on profesional level cars.<P>As for Fiero Stores headers I at least knew when I ordered them I would get them! I knew I would get a quality made product, I knew I would have no problems fitting them reguardless of trany type.<P>I bought peace of mind.<BR>Not horse power hype!<P>As I figure the designers thought it out well, each tube is in progression with each other on the same cylinder bank. The only problem would be encountered if the tubes going to the Y pipe are equaldistant they however are not.<P>The fireing order of the 2.8 is 123456 as this stands it would come to reason that each progressive fireing would cause a sonic resonance of the next cylinder of the same bank.<BR> <BR>This would scavenge the exhaust pulses in fireing order from the shared side of the engine.<P>If it were to simply make money, they could have made curves from each exhaust port directly to the collector and made each tube as short as possible. Less material more profit, less design time more profit, cheaper manufactureing company more profit.<P>It doesn't make sense to have a english formula 1 company fabricate headers for you when you could have billy bob blowtourch rig you up a set correct???? They are iregularly shaped for a purpose.<P>GT 40's used 180 headers they are a nightmare to work on! (I have not personaly worked on one) <P>Basicaly for a street car get what is easiest to install . The baloney about equal length tubeing and specific diameter of port configurations, and so forth, for a street car is virtually meaningless, because ultimately you will have to muffle the exaust some way. All that tuning goes down the crapper in the muffler.<P>I rarely go off but, some ya'll are strung a little tight. <P>Just my 2 cents.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||05-19-2000||02:07 PM||||Not so much high strung just why waste your money when you can spend less and get a better product. BBK, Lingenfelter, DC Sports, Neuspeed, Kamikaze, and LOTS of others all make equal length headers for Hondas, Mustangs, Camaros, Vetts, and more even HKS, Greddy, and APEXi make equal length header type manifolds for turbo cars..  It makes a difference... it brings back the torque you lost in opening up your exhaust for the HP gain. but why spend $550 + shipping when you can spend $522 delivered for a better set of headers. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FIEROCIOUS||05-20-2000||02:44 AM||||Get your tape measure!<P>Now measure any of the above listed headers you may be suprised, I may be suprised for that matter.<P>I have a Neuspeed header for my Civic lost 3 HP through out entire RPM band gained two at 6000 and above, well worth the 400.00 + I spent you be the judge? I'll be sure to measure them tonight! <P>I was however one of the first people to purchase them, and they are of the highest quality, again I bought a well made well fitting header.<P>I will accept a variation of + or - one half inch as "equal length".<P>So how does the finish hold up on the Sprint headers?||||reg||12
Z||000006||FIEROCIOUS||05-20-2000||02:52 AM||||As for DC sports, Nuespeed, Kamakaze, (depending on which model) are tri Y headers and would not work properly if they were equal in length.<P>They add torque due to this design not due to equal length.<BR> <BR>Post a pick of a "TRUE" equal length header. <P>And again it goes to crap in the muffler!<BR>If you run with a open pipe they are worth the trouble, but how many of us run with open pipes on the streets?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phaeton||05-20-2000||12:21 PM||||HA HA HA HA<BR>I'm sorry, sometimes I get amused way too easily.<BR>Turbulent airflow even gives the supercomputers a really hard time so most practical designs are from trial and error.<BR>Good information comes from places that have done extensive back to back comparisons of designs, time after time, keeping meticulous records.<BR>Not easy , not cheap, and not done very often. Most headers are made for looks and universal fit.<BR>Different camshafts want different header volumes.  Head porting changes header requirments.<BR>So correct design and a torch will produce better power than any of the "bolt on" headers.  Yes, even through mufflers, in fact, especially through mufflers!<BR>Ouch, ow, I said I was sorry.||||reg||12
Z||000008||FIEROCIOUS||05-21-2000||03:57 AM||||Phaeton, could't agree with you more!||||reg||1
